other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-03-09T11:09:31Z","updated_at":"2020-03-09T11:09:31Z","body":"@brunobat thanks for the feedback. \r\n\r\nThe documentation just means that if you want to activate the swagger ui in prod you have to always include it by setting the appropriate property to `true`.\r\n\r\n \r\nSince the swagger-ui configurations are not overridable in runtime i.e (the configs are only used during application build time), you can still activate them via build system props during app packaging as shown below:\r\n\r\nIf you have in your `application.properties` something like:\r\n```\r\n....\r\nquarkus.swagger-ui.always-include=false \r\n``` \r\n\r\n```\r\nmvn clean install -Dquarkus.swagger-ui.always-include=true \r\njava -jar <your-app-runner.jar>\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/596464052/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"machi1990","id":10106536,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTA2NTM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10106536?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990","html_url":"https://github.com/machi1990","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990/following